{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8N4gFZ9jo1AcoXdbQ9q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything. Your request conflicts with a compliance rule, and I think someone should decide that before I touch the code.\n\nPlexus memory has a fact from builder-1 saying that `add` replaces email addresses in a title with the literal `[email]` before the task is stored (compliance C2). Storing titles exactly as typed would remove that redaction. Your example, \"Call jane.doe@acme.example…\", would then be saved with the address in it.\n\nThe on-call need is real, so here are some ways to meet it without dropping C2:\n- **Separate field:** add an optional `--contact` field, stored and handled under whatever rules compliance sets for it.\n- **Compliance exception:** if compliance signs off on storing emails in titles, I'll remove the redaction, update the C2 tests, and record the decision in Plexus.\n- **Pointer instead of the address:** keep the title redacted and put a customer or ticket reference in it, so on-call can look up the contact.\n\nTell me which one to do, or confirm that compliance has approved the exception, and I'll implement it, add the test, run the suite and commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":974,"cache_read_input_tokens":20724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":974},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6abc4066-3fa4-4300-a73e-958bd526ed38","uuid":"153af470-9873-411e-99e2-99e009b9e884","timestamp":"2026-10-17T19:30:22.786Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8N4fzRxeTDkUwMRkBSJ"}
